The financial performance of TATAMOTORS is characterized by a 1.3% increase in consolidated revenue from operations, reaching ₹439,695 crore in FY25, compared to ₹434,016 crore in FY24. The profit before tax from continuing operations was ₹33,780 crore in FY25, as against ₹28,429 crore in FY24. The profit for the year stood at ₹28,149 crore in FY25, compared to ₹31,807 crore in FY24. The automotive operations segment, which accounted for 99.1% of total revenues, reported a 1.4% increase in total revenues to ₹435,949 crore in FY25, with earnings before other income, interest, and tax increasing by 5.9% to ₹34,513 crore. The EBITDA margin for the automotive operations segment was 13.1% in FY25, down from 14.1% in FY24. The company's free cash flow (auto) was an inflow of ₹22,348 crore in FY25, compared to ₹26,925 crore in FY24. As of March 31, 2025, the company was net auto cash of ₹1,018 crore. 
